<!--- applicable credit cards--->
<div class="tab-pane ${pdict.selectedPayment != 'PAYPAL' ? 'active' : ''} credit-card-content" id="credit-card-content" role="tabpanel">
  <iscomment>
    Payer Auth Setup and Device Data Collection run as soon as the shopper finishes the card block,
    i.e. before the billing form is submitted. This container carries the endpoints and hosts the
    hidden collection iframe.

    It sits here rather than in creditCardForm.isml because that template is inside the
    .credit-card-form fieldset, which is hidden for registered shoppers who have stored cards - and
    stored cards use this flow too. Its presence is what enables the early flow, so it never reaches
    the My Account "add card" page, which shares flexMicroform.js but has no basket.

    Which secure acceptance types are in scope is decided by
    PayerAuthSetupHelper.supportsEarlySetup, the same function the server routes use, so the two
    cannot drift. Silent post and the hosted flows keep the order-time setup route.
  </iscomment>
  <isscript>
    var cybPayerAuthHelper = require('*/cartridge/scripts/helper/PayerAuthSetupHelper');
    var cybEarlyPayerAuth = dw.system.Site.getCurrent().getCustomPreferenceValue('IsCartridgeEnabled')
        && cybPayerAuthHelper.supportsEarlySetup();
  </isscript>
  <isif condition="${cybEarlyPayerAuth}">
    <isscript>
      var cybPayerAuthCardTypes = cybPayerAuthHelper.getPayerAuthEnabledCardTypes().join(',');
    </isscript>
    <iscomment>
      data-payer-auth-card-types carries the card types with csEnablePayerAuthentication switched on,
      read from the same active payment cards CardHelper.PayerAuthEnable inspects. The client skips
      the setup request altogether for anything not in this list, so a card that does not need payer
      auth never costs a round trip. The route re-checks server side regardless.
    </iscomment>
    <div id="cyb-payerauth-ddc"
         data-setup-url="${URLUtils.https('CheckoutServices-PayerAuthSetupData')}"
         data-save-device-data-url="${URLUtils.https('CheckoutServices-SaveDeviceData')}"
         data-clear-url="${URLUtils.https('CheckoutServices-ClearPayerAuthSetup')}"
         data-capture-context-url="${URLUtils.https('CYBSecureAcceptance-FlexCaptureContext')}"
         data-payer-auth-card-types="${cybPayerAuthCardTypes}"
         hidden></div>
    <iscomment>
      SA_FLEX loads jQuery, payerAuthDDC.js and its own flexMicroform.js from creditCardForm.isml, so
      that jQuery sits immediately before the file that builds the microform. Loading it twice on one
      page replaces window.$ mid-flight, so only one of the two places may do it.

      jQuery has to be a synchronous tag either way: SFRA serves main.js and every assets.addJs script
      with defer, so $ does not exist yet this far up the body.
    </iscomment>
    <isif condition="${CsSaType != 'SA_FLEX'}">
      <script src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/custom/lib/jquery/jquery-3.7.1.min.js')}" type="text/javascript"></script>
      <script src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/custom/payerAuthDDC.js')}" type="text/javascript"></script>
      <script src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/custom/payerAuthCardFields.js')}" type="text/javascript"></script>
    </isif>
  </isif>

  <fieldset class="payment-form-fields">
    <!--- payment method is credit card --->
    <input type="hidden" class="form-control"
            name="${pdict.forms.billingForm.paymentMethod.htmlName}"
            value="${pdict.selectedPayment != 'PAYPAL' ? 'CREDIT_CARD' : 'PAYPAL'}"
    >

    <!--- register/authenticated user --->
    <isif condition="${pdict.customer.registeredUser}">
        <div class="user-payment-instruments container ${pdict.customer.registeredUser && pdict.customer.customerPaymentInstruments.length ? '' : 'checkout-hidden'}">
            <!--- Stored user payments --->
            <div class="stored-payments">
                <isinclude template="checkout/billing/storedPaymentInstruments" />
            </div>

            <!--- Add new credit card button --->
            <div class="row">
                <button class="btn btn-block add-payment btn-outline-primary" type="button">${Resource.msg('button.add.payment', 'checkout', null)}</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </isif>

    <fieldset class="credit-card-form ${pdict.customer.registeredUser && pdict.customer.customerPaymentInstruments.length ? 'checkout-hidden' : ''}">
        <isinclude template="checkout/billing/creditCardForm" />
        <isif condition="${pdict.customer.registeredUser}">
            <button class="btn btn-block cancel-new-payment btn-outline-primary ${pdict.customer.registeredUser && pdict.customer.customerPaymentInstruments.length ? '' : 'checkout-hidden'}" type="button">${Resource.msg('button.back.to.stored.payments', 'checkout', null)}</button>
        </isif>
    </fieldset>
  </fieldset>
</div>
